# Lucid-format checkpoints — same reason as the line above: a doctest or a
# stray script writing one into the tree must not become a commit.
*.lucid
# Two artefacts that reappear in the repo root after a commit, written by
# something in the hook chain that calls ``lucid.save`` with a bare relative
# path.  Ruled out: the serialization tests and doctests, the audit suite,
# check_numpy_h4 / check_docstring_{coverage,xrefs}, build_model_summaries,
# validate_model_zoo, a plain ``import lucid`` and pytest collection.  The
# writer is still unidentified — this entry stops them reaching a commit, it
# does not explain them.  Neither has ever been committed.
